WEBVTT

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.580
Hey, guys!

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:29.700
Those are some outfits you fly in!

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.990
Big Sis!

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:36.660
Big Sis! Big Sis! Big Sis!

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:38.810
Oh, you!

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:41.160
Long time no see, Big Sis! Doing good?

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:46.740
Yeah! Real good! You never change, huh?
You're always so spunky!

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.910
Because that's my specialty!

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.910
Hey, hey!

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:51.580
Commander, who's that?

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.790
Oh, right... Amatsuka?

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:56.370
Coming!

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:08.290
Probably should have done this first.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:13.700
Valkyrie Yayoi Amatsuka and three others,
reporting for duty at Tateyama!

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:14.790
Three others?

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:17.790
Come on, Yayoi Squad!

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.740
We three are...

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.040
...Big Sis' Shield Squadron.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.290
Mm-hmm. It's a pleasure.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:32.540
Again, this is way too much. Huh?

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.330
Ugh! The idiots found rivals!

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:44.080
I guess we're in your care now,
my naughty little sisters.

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:16.370
Valkyries' Bath

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:16.370
Fundoshi Fools Prohibited

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:16.370
No Men Allowed

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.870
Ahhhh! Feels so good!

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:18.870
Episode 5
 Tateyama Joint Forces !

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:21.200
Quit making dumb noises.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:27.700
Can't help it! A nice bath
turns everyone into an idiot!

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.830
Huh? What?

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:34.200
Nothing. Just impressed
you can bathe without drowning.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.150
You making fun?!

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:36.200
Ah...

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:41.080
She's right, though.
Azu, wanna practice swimming in the bath?

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.870
I hope you prune, idiot.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:49.870
By the way, Azuzu...
How do you know that Amatsuka Valkyrie?

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:52.700
Why do you assume I do?

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:57.830
She was friendly with Miyako.
I figured you knew her too.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:01.830
Stop thinking me and this idiot are a set.

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:04.950
But yeah, I know her.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:09.120
I flew with Amatsuka a bunch at our last base.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:13.080
It's amazing how she makes
that huge plane look agile.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:16.910
Yeah. I only caught a glimpse,
but she seems skilled.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:23.160
Big Sis moves to bases all over
with that same squad of hers.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:26.830
Always fighting? And why call her Big Sis?

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:32.040
Everyone does. I do too
'cuz I like it! Isn't it cool?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:36.370
Amatsuka and her crew
always fight in the hot zones.

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:39.620
Makes you wonder why they came here.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:41.040
Me! Me! Me!

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:42.040
What?

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.700
Why don't we ask her in person?

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:48.740
Oh, there you are! Care if I join in?

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:50.450
Yeah! Of course!

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:53.740
Oh? Is it just you three?

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:58.740
Sonoka said she wasn't feeling well
and left after showering.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:01.120
Hmm? I see.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:06.740
Well, in that case, I'll just have
to be content with you guys!

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.330
Huh?

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:11.080
--Poke!
--Eep! You pervert!

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:14.410
Aww! You're as innocent as ever, Azu!

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.240
Shuddap!

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:17.410
Can I ask something, Big Sis?

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:19.040
Huh? What?

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:22.990
Doesn't your squad always
go to dangerous places?

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:24.040
Yeah.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:27.580
Then, what did you come to Tateyama for?

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:32.740
Good question.
I'm sure you'll hear it from Satomi, but...

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:35.450
A counteroffensive?

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:38.990
Yup. That's the reason we're here.

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:44.040
You say "counteroffensive,"
but what's the target?

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:46.160
Isn't it obvious?

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.990
Fuji Primary Pillar.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:54.290
That's bullshit! What about
North America two years ago?!

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:59.580
Wasn't that lesson enough?!
Just how many Valkyries died?!

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:02.700
But there must be a reason for it.

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:08.200
Otherwise, why would they even plan it?
Do you know why?

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:11.410
It's surprising how much you notice.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:18.290
It's like Miko says. For this plan,
the brass have earned Odin's cooperation.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:21.870
That god will finally get off his butt and help.

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:23.950
He will?

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:26.660
Where are you going?

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:31.490
You can't tell?
To pay that cynical brat a special visit!

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:35.410
I need to talk with Odin too. Let me come.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:37.660
As long as you stay out of my way.

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:43.660
Good grief. What a fussy bunch.

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:45.620
Aren't you going too?

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:49.290
Odin doesn't like me much anyways.

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:52.870
By the way...

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.200
What?

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.540
Did something happen with Sonoka?

00:06:57.370 --> 00:07:01.620
You really notice everything, don't you?

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:03.990
What do you mean by "special visit"?

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:08.370
Isn't it obvious? I'm gonna put
my fist in his pretentious face!

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:12.290
Sounds like something Miyako would say.
How will you find him?

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:15.540
Erk! Well...

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:19.080
Claudy, do Named get some perk to call him?

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:20.990
I've never tried it.

00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:21.950
I see.

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:22.800
Now Showing

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:24.160
Whoa!

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:26.790
I guess it <i>is</i> a Named perk.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:30.410
Perfect! Just what I wanted! Let's go!

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:36.870
I've been waiting! What lovely
daughters to visit me on your own!

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:39.950
Come, give your father a hug!

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:43.450
Don't make me keep saying it.
I'm not your daughter, so stop--

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:47.540
Hold up! Save the usual routine for later!

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:51.990
We need to talk. What's the deal
with this counteroffensive?

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:55.790
Oh? Everyone knows about it already?

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:59.830
Or is our Named here getting special treatment?

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:01.910
Well, Claudia?

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:07.080
If I did get special treatment,
I'd have you answer her question.

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:09.410
Such a selfless daughter.

00:08:09.410 --> 00:08:11.580
So, what's your question?

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:17.200
I already said--the counteroffensive.
How did you swindle the brass?

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:20.370
How insulting for you to suggest that!

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:23.830
All I did was help come up with the plan.

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:26.740
Say, let's play a game while we talk.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:30.410
It's a fun way to bond with my daughter.

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:31.120
Screw--

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:33.950
If you won't, I refuse to talk.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:40.200
What can I say? I'm a bit immature.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:46.790
The plan is to attack the Fuji Primary Pillar
during the dormant period.

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:50.580
As in the cycle when Pillars are less active?

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:54.410
I thought we couldn't tell
when it starts and ends.

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:58.910
We deduced it through
the painstaking efforts of scientists...

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:01.870
...and the gift of my god powers.

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:06.660
Your Komagome Theory came in handy too.
You live up to your genius.

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:08.410
Shuddap and continue!

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:10.080
With talking or the game?

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:11.370
The talking!

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:12.580
Anyways,

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:18.290
all the sweat and tears paid off,
and we know the next Pillar to go dormant.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:20.790
It's the Fuji Primary Pillar.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:26.370
Thus, the counteroffensive.
You're certain enough to risk an attack?

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:31.660
I guarantee the Pillars will be less active.
You have this god's word.

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:37.540
However, no matter how deep its sleep,
Pillars will wake when attacked.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:39.790
It will be a fierce fight.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:44.540
Therefore, Japan has been
gathering strength for the battle...

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:48.240
...and has invited
the best of the best from afar.

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:50.830
The best of the best? You mean--

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:53.790
Yes. My beloved daughters.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:58.240
Being too smart causes your defeat.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:02.160
Having too many choices delays your judgment.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:05.620
That's why you're shot
down so much. It'll kill you.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:08.120
This game says nothing about me!

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:12.830
It's just a game, yet your flaws are glaring.

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:18.120
You're mediocre as a Valkyrie,
but your mind's a rare gem.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:21.410
You'd be happier somewhere you could use it.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:23.790
You don't think...?!

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:28.240
You don't think I know that?!

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:31.330
But, I...

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:36.790
At this rate, you'll run out of tears soon.

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:37.990
Odin!

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:40.620
Whoops! Wouldn't want
two of my daughters to hate me.

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:42.370
"Pillar of Manhood"

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:42.540
Whoops! Wouldn't want
two of my daughters to hate me.

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:47.660
I heard what I came for. For now,
I'll go along with the counteroffensive.

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:50.410
I'll keep in mind what you told me too.

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:52.330
Good, that's smart.

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:54.370
Azuzu, you okay?

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:59.490
I'm fine. It's just the wise words
of a scheming, soulless god.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:02.700
I see. I need to ask something too.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:07.910
Was my being moved here
related to the counteroffensive?

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:14.200
You're clever. The power of a Named
is vital to defeat a Primary Pillar.

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:19.240
With Ortlinde's death,
the country needed a replacement weapon.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:21.910
So that's how it is.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:28.490
Now then, go get your beauty sleep.
It's time to leave, my beautiful daughters.

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:30.910
Go with Asgard's blessing.

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:33.990
Did you say something?

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:38.660
Just wishing you well.
Take care of yourself, Claudia.

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:45.290
But remember this...
Valhalla's gate is always open to you.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:48.690
Now Showing

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:51.370
You think? He's always that way.

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:56.080
For real? I've never heard him
blabber like that before.

00:11:56.910 --> 00:12:00.540
Do you agree with what he said about me?

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:04.160
I don't think having choices is a bad thing.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:06.450
While it's true you're shot down a lot...

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:07.120
Hey!

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:10.290
We're a team to make up for that.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.700
Miyako would say the same.

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:15.370
Argh, dammit!
You sound just like that idiot now!

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:18.240
Don't turn into an idiot too!

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:21.870
Thanks for standing up for me.

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:25.330
G'nite.

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:32.080
Good grief. You're not
very true to your feelings.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:49.830
Sigururi.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:54.080
Sigururi.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:57.990
This plan is the real deal.

00:12:57.990 --> 00:13:04.490
However, it's a counteroffensive based on
a plan from the shadiest of sources.

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:10.950
Basically, all of Japan is attacking
Fuji Primary Pillar as it sleeps.

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:13.410
Sounds pretty simple, right?

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:22.200
Here's hoping for a successful
mission with Big Sis!

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:21.080
Seaside Kitchen
Fish Land

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:23.290
Cheers!

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:24.790
"Popular Menu!!
Fresh Fish and More!"
"Tomiura Seafood Bowl - SOLD OUT"

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:24.790
"Limited Availability"

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:25.870
"Fried Bartail Flathead - SOLD OUT"

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:28.790
It seems like a popular place.

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:30.950
Talk about a huge wait!

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:34.410
Order before it's all gone!
I want a Hearty Meal!

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:36.120
It's first come first served?

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:41.370
Don't know what to get?
In that case, I recommend...

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:42.830
...the black cod!

00:13:42.830 --> 00:13:43.910
Ooh!

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:46.740
Black... cod?

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:49.520
"Big Catch"

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:51.450
Mm-hmm. I'll have that.

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:53.080
--Hey, hey!
--Whoa!

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:56.330
Wow! Claudy's such a hero!

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:58.580
Just so you know, the black cod is--

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:00.410
It'll be a surprise!

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:02.160
Wh-What?

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:03.240
Not cool.

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:04.540
Huh?

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:06.160
Here, here!

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:07.990
O-Oh, thanks.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:08.580
Here!

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:09.080
Huh?

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:09.580
Here!

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:10.620
Thanks!

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:14.540
You're always so thoughtful! Wanna be my wife?

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:18.990
Wow! What do I say to that? Huh?

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:22.080
Just kidding. I wouldn't take her from you.

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:24.370
W-We're just together a lot.

00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:26.580
Together, huh?

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:32.040
Weren't you sent to the same place
after disobeying orders?

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:35.490
We sure were! I was so surprised!

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:38.120
What a coincidence, huh?

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:43.490
Azu could've picked to be sent anywhere
or even retired if she wanted to.

00:14:43.490 --> 00:14:46.160
Well the same goes for you.

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:49.910
Thank you for waiting!

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:52.200
Ooh!

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.450
Huh?

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:58.330
Th-This is...!

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:02.450
You're my hero! Lemme help you
pick out the bones, Claudy!

00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:05.720
"Legendary Rare Fish (1 ONLY)"
"Black Cod - SOLD OUT"

00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:04.080
Yoink! Yoink! Yoink!

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.950
You're really good at that.

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:09.160
Miyako, would you like to be my wife?

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:10.660
What should I do?

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:17.950
I could've retired, yet didn't.
Being told that really digs deep.

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:13.990
I want you to pick out fish bones for me.

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:17.950
That's the least romantic proposal ever!

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:21.910
Azu and I might be more alike than I thought.

00:15:21.910 --> 00:15:23.620
Azu isn't...!

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:27.700
Sono, you don't have
to say anything for my sake.

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:29.370
But...

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:31.950
But if it's for yourself, feel free.

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:34.120
Okay.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:39.660
What do you think about the counteroffensive?

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:45.160
The big wigs are serious about it.
We're more powerful than ever.

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:49.290
They're really hoping to
topple Fuji and liberate Japan.

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:58.200
However, Odin being gung-ho about
the whole thing doesn't sit right with me.

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:01.700
In other words, you don't trust Odin?

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:07.290
He's an interesting guy, and
I'm thankful for his help, but I don't trust him.

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:08.450
Do you?

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:14.160
Being a god, it's impossible
to tell what Odin is thinking, but...

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:15.620
But?

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:19.490
As far as I know,
he's earnestly supporting the plan.

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:22.120
Yeah? Did he tell you that?

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:27.740
I don't know his reasons, but he wants
to destroy the Pillars as much as we do.

00:16:27.740 --> 00:16:30.200
I want to believe in the plan.

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:35.490
Okay, that's enough!
No talking difficult stuff while we eat!

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:37.830
We haven't got to the difficult stuff!

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:42.200
Well it's difficult to me!
I'm not a smarty-pants like you!

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:43.950
Why are you mad at me?!

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:48.660
I don't know much about Odie,
but the plan uses the dormant period, right?!

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:54.830
So when the time comes and
it's our time to shine, fight with all you've got!

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:59.660
Face your problems with all your heart,
and it'll open up new doors!

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:00.910
See?!

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:02.200
Wha--?!

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.370
Like Claudy's black cod!

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:07.540
You ate it all?!

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:11.200
Huh? Yeah. It was so fatty,
I couldn't stop eating.

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:16.490
There's only so much fat one can eat!
I gave up after one bite!

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:22.620
Face your problems head-on, huh?
Your youthfulness is so inspiring.

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:25.700
Aren't you barely older than we are?

00:17:26.410 --> 00:17:32.120
Valkyries like us don't usually live very long.
I'm pretty much middle-aged.

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:35.240
Please excuse me. I'm going back to the base.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:36.870
You sure left a lot.

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:38.040
You can have it.

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:39.490
Why, thank you!

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:40.830
That's all you gotta say?!

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:43.200
Uh, that was a bust.

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:45.370
Hey, what were you plotting?

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:47.740
Something to do with Sonoka?

00:17:47.740 --> 00:17:49.410
Well...

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:56.490
Miko was trying to smooth things
over between Sonoka and me.

00:17:56.490 --> 00:17:58.950
For you and Sonoka?

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:04.790
We were once in the same squadron.
It's a complicated relationship.

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:12.660
Why... after all this time?

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:14.490
Big Sister...

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.330
Hmm?

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:25.490
Trying to give me a heart attack, Watarai?

00:18:25.490 --> 00:18:32.200
Good grief. This is my office, you know?
I'm kinda the highest-ranked person on base.

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:37.330
The door wasn't locked. You're pretty careless.

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:44.290
"909th Air Squadron
Commander Ichiro Satomi"

00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:42.620
You sneaked in just to tell me that?
I didn't forget to lock it.

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:48.830
It's always open in case lost
little girls have nowhere to go.

00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:50.740
I'm not a lost girl.

00:18:50.740 --> 00:18:54.540
I never said I was talking about you.

00:18:54.540 --> 00:18:56.040
Meanie.

00:18:56.040 --> 00:18:58.870
Sorry I kept quiet about Amatsuka.

00:18:58.870 --> 00:19:02.450
Orders came from above. They never asked me.

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:09.330
If you were following orders,
I understand. I'm a soldier too.

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:12.160
A 14-year-old soldier, huh?

00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:18.580
Seeing you guys, it breaks
the hearts of us pathetic adults.

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:22.330
There's not enough of us left,
and we're on the way out.

00:19:22.310 --> 00:19:24.330
"Dan Dan Noodles"

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:26.990
I'm sorry.

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:29.990
Are you asking for forgiveness?

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:44.410
Sorry to intrude. I'm leaving.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:48.950
Okay. Swing by whenever you like.

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:50.450
I won't anymore.

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:52.240
You always say that.

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:56.120
Meanie.

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:06.040
Not being forgiven is what saves me.

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:08.830
What an awful person I am.

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:21.790
This wears me out.

00:20:23.830 --> 00:20:29.120
120 seconds until Fuji Primary Pillar
enters a dormant state.

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:31.040
Will it actually stop?

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:34.490
That's what the brass and that god are saying.

00:20:34.490 --> 00:20:36.200
We'll know soon enough.

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:39.950
Be alert for any movement. Plane status?

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:44.910
They're in perfect shape, scaredy-cat.
The wings can fly whenever.

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:50.160
The rest is up to the Valkyries.
You just gotta whip 'em into action.

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:50.990
True.

00:20:50.990 --> 00:20:52.870
Ah, I'm so nervous!

00:20:52.870 --> 00:20:58.450
C-Calm down, idiot!
W-We'll see what happens any second!

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:04.120
Sonoka, you okay?

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:05.450
Huh?

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:11.870
Something on your mind?
If so, you can talk to me. We're a team.

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:16.450
You sound like Miko now.

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:18.660
Azuzu said that too.

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:21.910
Seems like you're totally one of us now.

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:24.290
Really? That's...

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:25.870
Scary to hear?

00:21:25.870 --> 00:21:29.330
No, that's not it.

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:33.700
It makes me happier than I thought it would.

00:21:37.160 --> 00:21:39.370
Say, Clo...

00:21:39.370 --> 00:21:42.160
20 seconds remaining!

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:48.240
Now Showing

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:52.490
13, 12, 11, 10...

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:57.790
...9, 8, 7, 6, 5...

00:21:57.790 --> 00:22:03.120
...4, 3, 2, 1, 0.

00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:14.290
As of now, the Primary Pillar has fallen asleep!

00:22:14.290 --> 00:22:21.080
Behold, my beloved daughters!
The curtains are opening for the decisive battle!

00:22:21.870 --> 00:22:24.950
Chief of gods, Odin, will watch over you!

00:22:26.660 --> 00:22:30.490
My brave warriors, it's the decisive battle!

00:22:30.490 --> 00:22:36.450
God of war, Odin, will watch over you!
The coming of Ragnarök is nigh!

00:23:57.740 --> 00:23:59.040
Argh! Not good!

00:23:59.040 --> 00:23:59.670
What?!

00:23:59.670 --> 00:24:01.830
It's the new Shield Squadron!

00:24:01.830 --> 00:24:03.120
Them?! Oh no!

00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:08.330
Yeah! They stole my character!
What do I have without my shades?!

00:24:08.330 --> 00:24:08.970
True!

00:24:08.970 --> 00:24:10.200
Not even a single hair!

00:24:09.550 --> 00:24:12.080
Next Time

00:24:09.550 --> 00:24:12.080
Episode 6
 Fuji Pillar Assault

00:24:10.200 --> 00:24:12.080
Gimme a break!
